WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.280
Gremlins 2, the new batch.

00:00:19.690 --> 00:00:27.900
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:28.920
I'm Mike.

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:31.380
I'm Sean. And I'm Joe.

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:33.960
Is there no back of the box?

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:36.800
Well, I think the new batch is like, you know, what are you going to do?

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:39.800
Are you going to also then attach something to that?

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:42.300
Oh, I don't know. Well, did they not?

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:43.420
I mean, come on, Mike.

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:44.520
You don't have to do it.

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:50.520
No, but I guess I'm saying like Gremlins 2, the new batch feels like the qualifier there.

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:51.960
No, that's just the name of the movie.

00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:54.140
Well, it's also the name of the game.

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:59.740
That's true. True. I use the back of the box as like some kind of exciting qualifier.

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:02.120
Okay. No, it's okay.

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:03.020
We don't need to do it anymore.

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:07.720
I feel like the, I feel like it was covered, but if you want the real back of the box, it

00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:10.940
was Gremlins 2, the new batch.

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:14.360
Can you stop the terrifying menace of the Gremlins?

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:20.980
Gremlins? I kind of just wanted you to stop it at, you said the new batch differently.

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:24.220
Gremlins 2, the new batch.

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:29.860
Yeah. I just want, I feel like you're, you made it sound like it was a weird thing to request,

00:01:29.960 --> 00:01:32.000
but that is the thing you've done for the past-

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:33.760
That's the thing you do. 400 episodes.

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:36.340
Maybe I'm just forgetting how I do the show.

00:01:36.980 --> 00:01:38.140
That thing you do.

00:01:38.380 --> 00:01:39.740
What do I do after that?

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:41.180
What do I do after the back of the box?

00:01:41.180 --> 00:01:42.420
I think it's the essential game list.

00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:44.300
Yeah. No. Oh, right.

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:45.400
The and welcome.

00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:46.980
Did I do that? You did.

00:01:47.260 --> 00:01:48.400
That's okay. Huh.

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:50.460
All right. Nevermind.

00:01:50.780 --> 00:01:55.080
Instead, Gremlins 2, the video game, the pitch meeting.

00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:58.260
Sean, what's your idea for a Gremlins 2 video game?

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:04.480
Um, I would be like, what should, maybe we should make a Gremlins 1 video game first.

00:02:04.940 --> 00:02:05.820
I love it.

00:02:05.960 --> 00:02:10.420
But I guess that's not a thing that we do around here, uh, vis-a-vis Goonies.

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:15.180
Um, but yeah, I mean, Gizmo's fun.

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:16.840
We want to play as Gizmo.

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:19.000
Hell yeah. Kids love Gizmo.

00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:20.560
I love it. It's in the game.

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:23.600
Joe, what's your idea for a Gremlins 2 video game?

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:28.240
It's hard now retroactively to come up with an idea now that I have this game in my

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:34.960
head. What I hope I wouldn't do, which they didn't do, is like a bunch of weird mini games that

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:39.400
are just specifically to get scenes exactly from the movie in it.

00:02:39.740 --> 00:02:45.180
So maybe it doesn't really answer your question, but I, I feel like that's what most people around

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:46.520
this era would have pitched.

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:48.540
And, uh, I would pitch this game.

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:53.020
I'm glad that they didn't release Gremlins 2 games, you know?

00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:58.160
And it's just like, it's just caveman games, but with Gremlins instead of cavemen.

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:02.040
Uh, so when was the last time you guys saw Gremlins 2?

00:03:02.340 --> 00:03:03.540
Right before this episode.

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:05.640
Oh, you did watch it.

00:03:05.820 --> 00:03:07.220
Right before this episode, baby.

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:08.700
Had you seen it before?

00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:10.360
I had seen enough.

00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:18.720
Enough. I had seen enough to know that Gremlins 2 is, as it implies, the new batch is just like

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:24.980
dialing up everything about Gremlins 1, except for saying, well, the only way to dial it up

00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:26.940
is by creating more Gremlins.

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:34.420
Like, there's just, there's a lot of different types of Gremlins that we never, like, I don't

00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:41.040
think we ever needed an electricity Gremlin or a vegetable Gremlin, but like, there they

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:42.100
are. They're in the movie.

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:47.280
They are there. I haven't seen it, but I gotta say, electricity Gremlin sounds pretty badass.

00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:50.880
Electricity Gremlin is in the game. Joe, did you see Gremlins?

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:54.600
No, I saw the original Gremlins like when I was a kid.

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:56.360
I remember almost nothing about it.

00:03:57.380 --> 00:03:59.800
It had a special place in my heart.

00:03:59.900 --> 00:04:01.320
I had a toy gizmo.

00:04:01.820 --> 00:04:02.880
I had the gizmo.

00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:05.760
Wait, did you have the gizmo that was also actually a Furby?

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:07.220
Well, here's the thing.

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:11.660
I'm only repeating information that was given to me.

00:04:11.780 --> 00:04:14.200
My mom would be like, you had a baby gizmo.

00:04:14.280 --> 00:04:17.200
And I was like, I don't remember having that stuffed animal mom.

00:04:17.480 --> 00:04:18.720
She's like, you had it.

00:04:18.860 --> 00:04:20.600
And so I just have to take her word for it.

00:04:20.700 --> 00:04:24.660
That's how I feel like when I have kids, I think I'm just gonna, when they're like 20,

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:27.340
I'll just tell them I got them all kinds of things for Christmas.

00:04:27.880 --> 00:04:28.840
Even if I didn't.

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:31.960
Yeah. It's probably, it's probably gonna work.

00:04:33.020 --> 00:04:36.180
I, I did own the gizmo that was actually a Furby.

00:04:36.340 --> 00:04:38.440
It did. It even had the ability to talk to the Furby.

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:39.640
Yeah. It was not a Furby.

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:44.540
Yeah. But it also, that also means that I got that gizmo in like 1999, like 2000.

00:04:45.020 --> 00:04:45.820
I guess. Yeah. That's weird.

00:04:46.120 --> 00:04:47.440
Was gremlins having a moment?

00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:49.140
Like they were like, oh, this is perfect.

00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:53.880
Yeah. I mean, I guess technically no one ever found out what happens when you get a Furby wet.

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:56.120
Oh. Is that true?

00:04:56.120 --> 00:04:58.520
No one's done it. Like, you know what I mean?

00:04:58.580 --> 00:04:59.560
Like, does it become a gremlin?

00:04:59.780 --> 00:05:00.800
Like maybe. Right.

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:05.400
Like the gizmo, did, did my gizmo have the ability to turn into a gremlin if I said it

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:07.340
past midnight? Like you definitely got your Furby wet.

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:11.420
You like, you definitely spilled that into the pool or something.

00:05:11.600 --> 00:05:13.360
I don't like the way you said that the first time.

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:14.600
I like the clarification.

00:05:17.620 --> 00:05:18.600
Eh, that's okay.

00:05:18.640 --> 00:05:19.460
Let's let that hang there for a bit.

00:05:19.460 --> 00:05:25.320
Moving on to the game. Do the graphics have any right to be this good?

00:05:26.280 --> 00:05:31.000
Like, I know we've seen good graphics on the NES and we've talked about the cut scenes

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:37.640
and certain things, but like the gizmo and the gremlin cut scenes and that wizard shopkeeper,

00:05:37.800 --> 00:05:40.340
his name is Mr. Wing, but whatever he looks like, he looks like a wizard.

00:05:40.880 --> 00:05:46.580
Like those scenes are like, I was like, did they expand the palette or the color palette

00:05:46.580 --> 00:05:47.680
or something for the NES?

00:05:47.800 --> 00:05:50.700
Like this is, those are really striking visuals.

00:05:51.180 --> 00:05:52.340
Yeah. They look pretty good.

00:05:52.340 --> 00:05:57.960
I thought you meant like, uh, the, the actual like gameplay graphics, which are, which are,

00:05:58.120 --> 00:06:00.300
which are pretty good, but nothing crazy.

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:07.920
I'd say as far as the gameplay graphics, they are as they are very, very good for what I'd

00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:14.320
expect a like licensed eighties movie video game to be, you know, based on our experience.

00:06:14.420 --> 00:06:18.440
Maybe I'm just like going to use this episode, just talk about how bad most other games based

00:06:18.440 --> 00:06:19.820
on movies are.

00:06:19.820 --> 00:06:22.520
Well, we played a lot of bad ones, but it's funny.

00:06:22.540 --> 00:06:27.500
You guys mentioned the, uh, actual gameplay graphics, because that was how I knew immediately.

00:06:27.500 --> 00:06:29.040
I didn't look at a manual or anything.

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:30.660
Just the look of the game.

00:06:31.020 --> 00:06:32.640
I knew it was a sun soft game.

00:06:32.800 --> 00:06:38.420
They have a look and sound to them in a way that I don't even know if like Konami and Capcom

00:06:38.420 --> 00:06:39.520
have like the same.

00:06:39.740 --> 00:06:40.540
Yeah. I get that.

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:46.600
Um, well, I, one thing that I liked about what they did was they made it very obvious

00:06:46.600 --> 00:06:50.880
that you are a small, like a small animal.

00:06:51.060 --> 00:06:54.760
Um, because like you're walking through hallways and like the doors are giant.

00:06:55.180 --> 00:06:58.100
And, um, I, I get what you mean too.

00:06:58.100 --> 00:07:05.480
Just like with the way that they like color things, like the way that they do like gradients,

00:07:05.720 --> 00:07:08.960
like it kind of feels the same as like blaster master and stuff.

00:07:09.180 --> 00:07:10.800
Yeah. I, I get that.

00:07:10.900 --> 00:07:17.360
I get that. And they also did the, the Batman video game, which was, uh, you know, tied to the movie

00:07:17.360 --> 00:07:21.880
as well. So like they, you know, they've got this thing where like, uh, you know, I recall you guys

00:07:21.880 --> 00:07:22.780
liking Batman a lot.

00:07:22.780 --> 00:07:26.460
So they got this thing where like, they're, they're not phoning in their movie licenses.

00:07:27.200 --> 00:07:28.460
Yeah, that's, that's for sure.

00:07:28.600 --> 00:07:31.160
And I didn't think that that stood out to me right away with this game.

00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:36.660
Even the, the way it looks, uh, first of all, while we're talking about being a small

00:07:36.660 --> 00:07:40.520
little creature, uh, is this the cutest walk cycle we've ever had?

00:07:40.520 --> 00:07:43.300
Like it's a waddle D movement, right?

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:49.560
Yeah. Like the, he, he is very, especially when he's walking sideways, it's just like this very

00:07:49.560 --> 00:07:50.780
adorable little waddle.

00:07:51.240 --> 00:07:56.420
Um, we haven't seen anything this cute since, um, our nostalgia bites episode, Antarctic

00:07:56.420 --> 00:07:57.640
Adventure with the penguin.

00:07:58.280 --> 00:07:59.480
Oh yeah. Ah, yes.

00:07:59.520 --> 00:08:01.420
The penguin was, uh, quite cute.

00:08:01.600 --> 00:08:07.540
But yeah. So the, the game, uh, doesn't do like a side scrolling platformer with gizmo.

00:08:07.540 --> 00:08:11.220
It does, uh, the isometric viewpoint, but not, not really.

00:08:11.340 --> 00:08:12.300
It's more like, it's kind of top.

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:13.380
It's not isometric.

00:08:13.700 --> 00:08:15.020
Yeah. Well, you know what I mean, right?

00:08:15.220 --> 00:08:16.420
It gives like a Zelda.

00:08:17.080 --> 00:08:21.820
Yeah. But it does give off a good sense of 3d, even though it's not with just the way that it

00:08:21.820 --> 00:08:24.280
has the shadow under your jump and stuff like that.

00:08:24.280 --> 00:08:28.820
So, you know, I think those things make or break these top down games.

00:08:28.900 --> 00:08:33.860
Cause there's a reason why in Zelda games outside of like maybe Link's Awakening or whatever,

00:08:34.120 --> 00:08:36.400
like you don't usually jump in those kinds of games.

00:08:36.440 --> 00:08:40.900
It's hard to track yourself, but this game, there's a lot of pitfalls and everything.

00:08:41.200 --> 00:08:47.280
So, you know, what do you guys think when it comes to making a, uh, top down platformer

00:08:47.840 --> 00:08:51.620
game, right? We usually experience platformers as side scrollers.

00:08:52.260 --> 00:08:53.280
Sure. Yeah.

00:08:53.580 --> 00:08:58.120
Um, the, the platforming in this game, it, I'm of two minds about it.

00:08:58.440 --> 00:09:00.440
Like you, the controls are tight.

00:09:00.620 --> 00:09:01.900
It's one to one for sure.

00:09:02.060 --> 00:09:08.160
Like, and you can control yourself in midair and you can, if you like really mess up a

00:09:08.160 --> 00:09:12.700
jump, you have enough control to even just like, Oh, I'm going to jump back to where

00:09:12.700 --> 00:09:18.700
I came from. Now that said, like between a lot of the things that they're doing with the platforms, like

00:09:18.700 --> 00:09:22.340
it's not just a solid ground and void.

00:09:22.340 --> 00:09:27.600
There's also like a conveyor belts and like rolling things.

00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:37.420
And so it can be, it can, it can be tough, especially when you're going sideways or, or, or sort of like diagonal.

00:09:37.420 --> 00:09:43.880
And I feel like when you go diagonal, you kind of go at double speed, but that might just be a me thing.

00:09:44.340 --> 00:09:47.400
Um, no, it's, it's there.

00:09:47.580 --> 00:09:50.140
It's, it's a little uneven, but it's, it's pretty good.

00:09:50.920 --> 00:09:57.420
I mostly had overall like really positive feelings about the platforming in this.

00:09:57.500 --> 00:09:59.700
Cause I think I'm used to top down games.

00:09:59.780 --> 00:10:05.420
Like you said, either not having a jump or like being, being bad at their platforming.

00:10:05.520 --> 00:10:06.540
And this felt really good.

00:10:06.700 --> 00:10:08.620
I did notice a little bit.

00:10:08.720 --> 00:10:15.120
Yeah. There was a little bit of a, um, annoying feedback difference when I was trying to go diagonally.

00:10:15.120 --> 00:10:22.980
That was like the one part of the, of the controlling that like really sort of bugged me, but I was overall really impressed with how precise it all felt.

00:10:23.160 --> 00:10:39.980
And, and the fact that they, they did this thing that a lot of companies, a lot of games don't do, which is like you said, allowing you to turn back in midair or to, to, to change direction in midair completely as easily as you would be able to, if you were, if you were on the ground.

00:10:39.980 --> 00:10:54.300
And I know that doesn't make any sense like in real life, but I think that it took a while for these game developers to realize that like to sacrifice it, making sense in real life in order to make it fun and feel good to play.

00:10:54.300 --> 00:11:10.640
And I've, I felt that this, I was very impressed with how this felt as a platformer that is, yeah, basically letting you move through, you know, what is fundamentally 3d space, even if it's obviously not really 3d, but it's like, you can go in all directions.

00:11:10.660 --> 00:11:11.940
It's not just a side scroller.

00:11:12.500 --> 00:11:15.720
So it, I was, I was pleased with the platforming overall.

00:11:16.660 --> 00:11:24.700
And Gizmo has a projectile as, as his main method of attacking or is really only method of attacking.

00:11:25.040 --> 00:11:26.740
I hated that at first.

00:11:27.220 --> 00:11:31.960
Uh, I, not that like a mad that Gizmo had, uh, like a gun.

00:11:32.100 --> 00:11:33.240
I, I, it's not really around.

00:11:33.380 --> 00:11:35.220
It's like, it's like, he starts with like a matchstick, right?

00:11:35.360 --> 00:11:36.800
Like, or whatever. That's the second thing.

00:11:36.920 --> 00:11:37.740
That's the first upgrade.

00:11:37.900 --> 00:11:40.260
Oh, okay. Was he throwing, like a ball or something?

00:11:40.500 --> 00:11:41.920
Or like, it's like a ball or something.

00:11:41.920 --> 00:11:44.160
Or something? Splurge of goop or something.

00:11:44.360 --> 00:11:45.540
He's spitting on the enemies.

00:11:45.840 --> 00:11:46.800
Something like that.

00:11:47.040 --> 00:11:48.220
Yeah. In like a weird arc-ing motion.

00:11:48.220 --> 00:11:50.340
In like a leftover wetness. But like.

00:11:50.340 --> 00:11:51.380
That created the Grims.

00:11:51.640 --> 00:11:53.100
It's not great at first.

00:11:53.100 --> 00:11:58.180
I think that the base weapon, um, feels a little frustrating to connect with enemies.

00:11:58.600 --> 00:12:04.780
Uh, and maybe it was just because those, uh, those tomatoes and spiders in the first level,

00:12:05.020 --> 00:12:09.420
like, have kind of sporadic movement, um, and can hop around and stuff.

00:12:09.420 --> 00:12:13.500
So it's not particularly helpful with a projectile, uh, weapon.

00:12:14.200 --> 00:12:17.780
But it did grow on me later on as you continue to, to, um.

00:12:18.320 --> 00:12:19.260
You get a better weapon.

00:12:19.720 --> 00:12:21.140
Yeah, yeah, yeah. You get the spread.

00:12:21.460 --> 00:12:24.940
Yeah, you know, but like, you know, once you have like more range with it, it feels better.

00:12:24.940 --> 00:12:26.960
But do you think that was the right call?

00:12:27.180 --> 00:12:30.740
Like, should that have been like a bonus power-up?

00:12:30.840 --> 00:12:32.180
Like a quick projectile thing?

00:12:32.300 --> 00:12:33.340
And he should have been a melee?

00:12:33.720 --> 00:12:35.440
Like, is that the right call for Gizmo?

00:12:35.780 --> 00:12:41.980
I don't think Gizmo, uh, it makes sense for him to be in much of a combat role at all.

00:12:42.120 --> 00:12:46.380
So if you're gonna make a game like this, I think like, you have carte blanche.

00:12:46.560 --> 00:12:47.480
Do whatever you need to do.

00:12:48.000 --> 00:12:49.960
Give him a gun. Give him an ammo count.

00:12:50.880 --> 00:12:58.040
Yeah, as someone that doesn't know really anything about Gremlins or has no attachment to this character, I thought it worked fine.

00:12:58.260 --> 00:13:01.420
But yeah, I don't know if it makes any sense at all.

00:13:01.460 --> 00:13:03.820
Yeah, he's like helpless, like in the movies.

00:13:04.340 --> 00:13:09.020
Yeah, but I do want to circle back to this first projectile.

00:13:09.260 --> 00:13:15.840
I'm pretty sure that is the reason it feels harder to hit is because it goes in an arcing, lobbing motion.

00:13:15.840 --> 00:13:23.120
Which I'm assuming was intentional because they wanted to feel like you're powering up and they succeeded in that.

00:13:23.540 --> 00:13:34.080
Uh, I do wonder if they succeeded in that by making your next gun feel better or just like maybe a little bit artificially making your first gun feel really bad.

00:13:34.400 --> 00:13:36.780
Yeah, I think I agree with both, Joe.

00:13:36.780 --> 00:13:45.060
I think like, it feels like it's, it feels like it's not the right way to handle combat in this game at the beginning.

00:13:45.060 --> 00:13:47.200
And then by the end of the game, it's like, it's fine, right?

00:13:47.300 --> 00:13:49.120
It's like, cool, this is what you do.

00:13:49.240 --> 00:13:50.260
And it's very easy.

00:13:50.300 --> 00:13:53.060
And you've got plenty of different ranges of attack.

00:13:53.240 --> 00:13:54.060
And so whatever.

00:13:54.300 --> 00:13:59.440
And plus there's fun other like, you know, little power ups you can have for like a hot second, like the pogo stick.

00:13:59.660 --> 00:14:03.360
I think that's cute. I don't recall gizmo on a pogo stick, but sure.

00:14:03.960 --> 00:14:05.580
Put him on one. Yeah.

00:14:05.720 --> 00:14:08.640
If his name's gizmo, he can be on a pogo stick and it makes sense.

00:14:08.880 --> 00:14:13.560
But Sean touched on something that I wanted to get to maybe later, but now feels like a good time too.

00:14:14.040 --> 00:14:19.280
Um, yeah, they made gizmo the main, uh, character of the game.

00:14:19.460 --> 00:14:20.400
Should they have done that?

00:14:20.560 --> 00:14:21.460
Or should it have been Billy?

00:14:21.700 --> 00:14:23.420
Like, should you know, it should have been gizmo.

00:14:23.760 --> 00:14:27.400
But like, you don't think you should be playing as like the scientist trying to stop the grimmons?

00:14:27.400 --> 00:14:29.260
Nobody remembers the guy.

00:14:29.600 --> 00:14:32.000
Everyone remembers gizmo in the grims.

