00:19:52.980 --> 00:19:53.880
Yeah, you know what I mean?

00:19:53.960 --> 00:19:56.060
It's like, it's just, why is there lava here?

00:19:56.060 --> 00:19:59.300
Or an office building with a bunch of spikes.

00:19:59.560 --> 00:20:00.900
Yeah, conveyor belts.

00:20:00.900 --> 00:20:03.700
Yeah. Yeah, conveyor belts and all that.

00:20:03.860 --> 00:20:04.920
It's like, I get it.

00:20:05.120 --> 00:20:08.760
It needs to be done to gamify the whole thing.

00:20:08.780 --> 00:20:10.640
And I'm not asking for them to tone it down.

00:20:10.860 --> 00:20:21.040
Just pointing out that that, you know, did feel, it did feel like a weird stretch for like what it could have just been, you know, like fully embraced the zaniness.

00:20:21.040 --> 00:20:28.980
Which I guess they did in some ways, because they're in the movie, they make a really strong tomatoes that like you can bounce like tennis balls.

00:20:29.280 --> 00:20:36.740
And of course, one of the gremlins eats the or drinks the tomato serum, and then becomes a vegetable gremlin.

00:20:37.020 --> 00:20:38.300
That was the one I mentioned earlier.

00:20:38.860 --> 00:20:42.240
So now there's big tomatoes that you have to fight in the first level.

00:20:42.580 --> 00:20:46.980
And they put their best foot forward, because it's like one of the first enemies you see in the game.

00:20:47.220 --> 00:20:50.400
Yeah, so they're letting you know that they also did their homework and watch.

00:20:50.400 --> 00:20:51.440
See, we watched the movie.

00:20:52.440 --> 00:20:53.440
We watched the movie.

00:20:53.580 --> 00:20:56.460
The tomatoes are core element and theme to the movie.

00:20:58.140 --> 00:21:02.980
But yeah, there is an emphasis in the game besides like fighting enemies.

00:21:03.180 --> 00:21:04.120
There is a lot.

00:21:04.300 --> 00:21:07.100
It's almost more platformer than action, right?

00:21:07.200 --> 00:21:13.980
There's a lot of, again, I'm going to say verticality, even though it's not side scrolling.

00:21:13.980 --> 00:21:19.380
It's, there's a lot of traps, pitfalls, Joe mentioned the lava, conveyor belts.

00:21:19.600 --> 00:21:24.200
It is really a movement based game more than a action game.

00:21:24.200 --> 00:21:32.180
Yeah, especially later in the game, when almost every surface that you're on turns into some kind of movement puzzle.

00:21:32.700 --> 00:21:33.880
That's a strong word.

00:21:33.980 --> 00:21:34.880
Puzzle is a strong word.

00:21:35.040 --> 00:21:46.440
But it seems like you can't let your guard down in these lighter levels, because you're always on a conveyor belt, or you're always dodging like a swinging mace.

00:21:46.440 --> 00:21:50.660
Or, so, it's kind of overwhelming.

00:21:51.660 --> 00:21:53.620
Like, I was very bad at these.

00:21:54.540 --> 00:22:02.580
I was also pretty bad at these, but compared to most other games that try to do this kind of thing, I feel like I wasn't as bad.

00:22:02.720 --> 00:22:07.880
You know, like, I feel like this felt fair, and I felt like I could learn it.

00:22:08.040 --> 00:22:09.480
And I felt like I did to a decent point.

00:22:09.540 --> 00:22:14.980
I only got to, like, stage four, the very beginning of it, and that's when I really started to, like, lose my mind and die.

00:22:14.980 --> 00:22:24.140
But, like, I feel like, given more time, like, this feels much more, beating this game feels more attainable than a lot of other NES platformers to me.

00:22:24.900 --> 00:22:29.120
Especially, like, enemy, like, enemy-ridden platformers.

00:22:29.260 --> 00:22:33.100
Yes. I mean, part of that is because it is a very short game, too.

00:22:33.220 --> 00:22:34.700
Yeah, right. Right.

00:22:34.800 --> 00:22:38.980
I agree with that, Joe. Also, because, like, the bosses aren't cheap or anything.

00:22:38.980 --> 00:22:47.340
In fact, even most of the enemies are not something that, like, they're not cheaply designed or they don't rush at you in a way that makes you lose health often.

00:22:47.440 --> 00:22:51.700
It's more like, you know, you have to just be cautious with Gizmo.

00:22:51.860 --> 00:22:55.840
You know, like, you almost have to play a little more defensive and not rush through.

00:22:56.000 --> 00:23:00.280
Or, I guess, like, if you're good at the game, just rush through these things as we don't have to deal with fighting them.

00:23:01.320 --> 00:23:04.560
But, like, the bosses are also, like, I don't know, they're fun.

00:23:04.560 --> 00:23:14.260
I like these, you know, these gremlin boss battles and they just, yeah, they kind of just take place in a space with just you and the gremlin and that gremlin's specific abilities.

00:23:14.640 --> 00:23:20.500
But it's not, I don't know, I didn't need, like, some big epic battle.

00:23:20.500 --> 00:23:25.120
I feel like it does feel kind of cool, this one-on-one fight with the gremlins when they finally arrive.

00:23:25.660 --> 00:23:27.260
They all have great art.

00:23:27.260 --> 00:23:46.200
There isn't, there just isn't really that much, like, mechanically happening, aside from kind of the electric one, which I found more annoying than fun because you can't really, I mean, you can kind of, in general, know where his projectiles are going to go.

00:23:46.440 --> 00:23:51.520
But it kind of gets random feeling and I didn't appreciate that.

00:23:51.920 --> 00:23:55.920
But, yeah, the bosses at least look cool.

00:23:55.920 --> 00:24:05.320
And there is a reason to kill enemies outside of the bosses and that is, of course, the crystal balls that you collect in order to buy things at the shop from Mr.

00:24:05.420 --> 00:24:10.100
Wing. You know, there's two ways to design these kinds of games.

00:24:10.140 --> 00:24:24.240
We've often seen where, like, you shoot the enemies, take them down, and then they drop, like, said power-up or said, you know, like, one-up or a certain amount of points or whatever.

00:24:24.240 --> 00:24:25.420
And then those things help you.

00:24:25.700 --> 00:24:32.820
Is it better to handle it with the randomness that way and encourage you to, you know, try different enemies?

00:24:32.820 --> 00:24:42.080
Or is it better this way where it's like everybody just has a set currency amount and then you just take that to the shop and redeem exactly what you want?

00:24:42.900 --> 00:24:45.220
I'm not sure which one is better.

00:24:45.360 --> 00:24:46.600
I guess it depends on what you want to design.

00:24:46.760 --> 00:24:52.820
But I do think that this game, you know, does the latter, but it does it in a weird way.

00:24:53.340 --> 00:24:59.440
Where it's not like, oh, okay, kill as many enemies so I can get enough currency to buy the things I want.

00:25:00.080 --> 00:25:05.680
Because really, after, like, the first or maybe the second level, you're going to have all the money you need.

00:25:05.860 --> 00:25:07.680
Yeah, it's a broken economy.

00:25:08.040 --> 00:25:13.260
Yeah, when you go to the shop, you can only buy one thing no matter what.

00:25:13.340 --> 00:25:15.420
Unless I missed some way to reopen the shop.

00:25:15.620 --> 00:25:18.920
No, you're right. Every time you come across the shop, you can only buy one thing.

00:25:19.080 --> 00:25:20.780
So it's not really about money management.

00:25:20.980 --> 00:25:26.460
It's more about, like, you get basically, like, every time you come across the shop, you get, like, one ticket to buy one thing.

00:25:26.680 --> 00:25:28.980
So it's more about managing what you're buying.

00:25:29.520 --> 00:25:33.920
Yeah, I just think, like, maybe they didn't intend it to be that way, but that's how it works out.

00:25:34.660 --> 00:25:42.420
Yeah, because having a, like, a price is moot if, you know, you're always going to have enough to buy the most expensive thing.

00:25:44.060 --> 00:25:52.200
Um, so the priority is usually, like, you've got to get your spread shot, and then if you, the next time you see it, you're going to want to heal whenever you want.

00:25:52.540 --> 00:25:54.420
Uh, I guess you could buy balloons, too.

00:25:54.640 --> 00:25:56.100
