00:25:56.900 --> 00:25:59.300
Um, do you guys remember what the balloons do?

00:25:59.560 --> 00:26:04.140
Don't they stop you from, when you fall in a pit, they, like, give you one free, like, you're okay?

00:26:04.140 --> 00:26:13.080
Oh, yeah, that's true. Yeah, they act like the, um, the Yoshi baby mode on some of the Mario games now, where, like, Yoshi can't die if he falls in a pit.

00:26:13.380 --> 00:26:14.740
Uh, he just comes back.

00:26:14.900 --> 00:26:18.040
It's the same thing. Well, good, because Yoshi always got the shirt on that stick.

00:26:18.480 --> 00:26:20.060
Yoshi cannot die, right?

00:26:20.220 --> 00:26:21.560
Yeah, it's canonically true.

00:26:21.880 --> 00:26:29.040
And also, speaking of the shop and everything, like, the things you buy from the shop are, like, you know, restoring your health and extra life.

00:26:29.040 --> 00:26:34.840
The cool stuff, like the, uh, pogo stick, you, you, you get those in the environment.

00:26:35.120 --> 00:26:41.580
So, you know, it's not like you can hold on to that kind of stuff, buy it now, and be like, oh, I'll save this for the boss fight or something.

00:26:41.780 --> 00:26:42.620
Like, that doesn't happen.

00:26:43.060 --> 00:26:52.060
I think that the bosses, like, I know we kind of went over them, that there's, yeah, again, like, not, not too mechanically much going on.

00:26:52.060 --> 00:27:05.840
But I don't even think the bosses were that hard compared to just the knockback of getting hit by an enemy, especially in those later levels we were talking about, because there just is so much void.

00:27:06.420 --> 00:27:12.060
But I guess, yeah, now that we're talking about items, uh, that's where those balloons come into play.

00:27:12.240 --> 00:27:14.720
So, it's kind of balancing itself out there.

00:27:15.320 --> 00:27:30.740
And those boss fights, uh, or even just, like, you know, uh, moments of you've arrived at your destination, uh, for whether you pick up a new item or enter a boss fight, for the most part, um, they just, they don't feel like you've reached the end of anything.

00:27:30.740 --> 00:27:37.060
The game just kind of, like, starts playing music and, uh, you know, like, you're just, you're just there now.

00:27:37.060 --> 00:27:38.340
And it's like, okay, that's fine.

00:27:38.360 --> 00:27:44.920
But what was really jarring is the final boss battle, uh, it's just like a, it's like a cut to black.

00:27:44.920 --> 00:27:50.940
And then you're just in the fight with, um, I don't know the, whatever, whoever the final gremlin dude is.

00:27:50.980 --> 00:27:53.700
Uh, but he's in, you know, he's in his, like, robot mech thing.

00:27:54.060 --> 00:27:57.020
And I guess that took a lot of pixel work or whatever.

00:27:57.340 --> 00:27:58.880
So there's no background.

00:27:59.160 --> 00:28:05.980
So it's just like, you were doing one thing and then you just, like, automatically are transported into this, you know, black hole space.

00:28:05.980 --> 00:28:11.840
Fighting this other, you know, and we've seen that in shmups, but in shmups, I guess it's more like, well, at least I'm in space or whatever.

00:28:12.020 --> 00:28:20.300
You're in space, yeah. Yeah, you know, now it's just like, I've entered some weird gremlin void where the gremlins and I only exist and nothing else.

00:28:20.700 --> 00:28:23.180
Oh, there was no cut scene before that?

00:28:23.200 --> 00:28:24.480
No cut scene that leads into it.

00:28:24.520 --> 00:28:26.180
Yeah, it just cuts right to the fight.

00:28:26.800 --> 00:28:28.940
