00:32:10.200 --> 00:32:13.120
I don't know if they treat them poorly, but they're, like, little Gremlins.

00:32:13.340 --> 00:32:15.240
Sean, we're at, like, 1,000 Pokemon.

00:32:15.240 --> 00:32:18.140
You can just say a name, and it's probably a Pokemon.

00:32:19.320 --> 00:32:21.380
Impodimp is 859.

00:32:21.620 --> 00:32:23.080
How about Bunga Bunga?

00:32:23.580 --> 00:32:25.280
Bunga Bunga, yeah, who could forget?

00:32:25.520 --> 00:32:26.420
The Caveman Pokemon.

00:32:27.860 --> 00:32:29.740
But Caveman didn't talk like that.

00:32:29.880 --> 00:32:31.700
I just, I want to get it on the screen again.

00:32:31.740 --> 00:32:37.100
How do we know? Caveman were actually probably smarter than us.

00:32:37.240 --> 00:32:39.700
I'm just going to throw it out there. They didn't waste their time making podcasts.

00:32:40.240 --> 00:32:41.220
That is true.

00:32:41.720 --> 00:32:43.740
We are an inferior being.

00:32:43.740 --> 00:32:46.580
Any other comments about Gremlins 2?

00:32:46.580 --> 00:32:47.940
The concept of Gremlins?

00:32:48.240 --> 00:32:50.860
I feel like I'm really surprised.

00:32:51.460 --> 00:32:56.420
Not that there weren't more video games or that we didn't get Gremlins 1 on the NES or anything.

00:32:56.500 --> 00:32:59.760
I just feel like it's kind of surprising Gremlins isn't still around.

00:33:00.080 --> 00:33:03.740
Like, getting killed to death in, like, the franchise reboot.

00:33:04.460 --> 00:33:06.160
It's only a matter of time.

00:33:06.160 --> 00:33:12.180
I'm sure there will be, like, a 3D animated, like, Smurfs-esque Gremlins movie at some point soon.

00:33:12.640 --> 00:33:14.560
But I have a question about Gremlins.

00:33:14.620 --> 00:33:19.340
This is always something that, like, I'm not clear on because it's been so long since I've seen the movie.

00:33:19.340 --> 00:33:22.540
But you can't feed the Gremlin after midnight?

00:33:22.780 --> 00:33:25.280
You can't feed the Mogwai after midnight.

00:33:25.520 --> 00:33:27.460
The Mogwai. That's what I mean. Joe, Joe, you keep getting tripped up.

00:33:27.460 --> 00:33:29.680
The Gremlins are already, yeah.

00:33:30.080 --> 00:33:31.540
They're from the point of no return.

00:33:31.660 --> 00:33:34.960
This is decades of me believing this.

00:33:35.080 --> 00:33:38.460
I'm trying to undo right now that the Gremlins are these cute things.

00:33:39.200 --> 00:33:41.280
It's like, you know, it was Dr.

00:33:41.780 --> 00:33:43.540
Frankenstein. That was Frankenstein's monster.

00:33:43.540 --> 00:33:44.720
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:33:44.980 --> 00:33:47.880
But is there something where you can't get them wet?

00:33:48.200 --> 00:33:50.060
Yeah, you can't spill water on them.

00:33:50.380 --> 00:33:53.340
So both of those things will cause them to spawn Gremlins?

00:33:53.420 --> 00:33:54.520
Yes, yes, exactly.

00:33:54.780 --> 00:33:57.260
Oh, it just seems like, just make it one of those things.

00:33:57.460 --> 00:33:58.940
No, no.

00:33:59.280 --> 00:34:01.420
Oh, okay. Just don't.

00:34:01.600 --> 00:34:02.600
Fair enough. Yeah.

00:34:04.020 --> 00:34:09.460
And if you spill water on any of us, it forms the Essential Games list.

00:34:13.060 --> 00:34:14.600
All right, so I'm going to be honest here.

00:34:15.400 --> 00:34:20.560
I like Gremlins, mostly because I owned a gizmo doll that was kind of like a Furby.

00:34:21.120 --> 00:34:22.520
And I took good care of it.

00:34:22.700 --> 00:34:23.960
Never really got it to do anything.

00:34:24.220 --> 00:34:26.480
Would love to do a whole tangent thing on Furbies.

00:34:26.480 --> 00:34:28.220
Like, could you actually ever teach them English?

00:34:28.360 --> 00:34:30.100
That was like a rumor. I don't think that's true.

00:34:30.800 --> 00:34:40.380
But that's not like, you know, my affinity and nostalgia for Gremlins can't possibly play a role because that's not the point of this podcast.

00:34:40.380 --> 00:34:50.520
So I went in actually with low expectations because, as Joe alluded to throughout his many comments on the show, we've been having some pretty bad movie tie-ins.

00:34:50.520 --> 00:34:52.120
I should have known, though.

00:34:53.380 --> 00:34:54.960
Sunsoft, you've done it again.

00:34:55.200 --> 00:34:56.460
You make good games.

00:34:56.720 --> 00:34:59.320
But mostly just play it.

00:34:59.440 --> 00:35:02.500
And I think that's where I'm winding up with Gremlins 2 here as well.

00:35:02.620 --> 00:35:04.740
I really enjoyed my time with it.

00:35:04.740 --> 00:35:11.580
But I'm not seeking to go back with it outside of reviewing it for this show.

00:35:11.580 --> 00:35:18.360
I guess I was just more surprised at how competent and pleasant it performed as a game.

00:35:18.500 --> 00:35:20.820
It was like, oh, Gizmo's fun to be.

00:35:20.820 --> 00:35:27.140
And the challenge is the right amount of like, it's hard, but it's achievable.

00:35:27.600 --> 00:35:32.360
So these are things that are actually kind of low praise when you think about it.

00:35:32.500 --> 00:35:36.960
But at this point in the catalog, it becomes high praise because we play so many bad games.

00:35:37.180 --> 00:35:44.480
So I'm settling in at Gremlins 2 is a play it and a solid play it as that, but doesn't quite reach the threshold of essential.

00:35:45.020 --> 00:35:46.840
Sean? Yeah, I agree.

00:35:48.460 --> 00:35:50.140
There's a lot of polish here.

00:35:50.760 --> 00:35:53.180
But it is still half-baked at its core.

00:35:54.520 --> 00:35:56.200
But, you know, you play as Gizmo.

00:35:56.200 --> 00:35:57.600
You fight the Gremlins.

00:35:58.460 --> 00:35:59.560
What's not to like?

00:35:59.760 --> 00:36:02.060
It's just not a lot to love.

00:36:02.520 --> 00:36:03.660
So, yeah, not essential.

00:36:04.080 --> 00:36:07.680
Joe? I also was very surprised at this.

00:36:07.760 --> 00:36:11.200
I mean, I guess you alluded to the fact that I alluded to this fact already.

00:36:11.440 --> 00:36:16.260
But I was very surprised that this was such a competent game.

00:36:16.260 --> 00:36:22.280
But I do think as I played it, you know, I recognized how polished it is and how well designed.

00:36:22.280 --> 00:36:28.380
I mean, not just the look of it is, but also the gameplay, the music is beautiful.

00:36:30.300 --> 00:36:36.040
And there are so many games on the NES that even games that I love that I have to go into it with this.

00:36:36.120 --> 00:36:42.460
Like, I got to put, like, sort of the glasses on of, like, I'm going to see this through the lens of, like, remember, this is an NES game.

00:36:42.460 --> 00:36:48.380
It doesn't have all the, like, modern, you know, luxuries that we might have now.

00:36:48.500 --> 00:36:50.140
It might not feel as good as a modern game.

00:36:50.220 --> 00:36:51.620
And then I love it for that.

00:36:51.820 --> 00:36:54.300
This game, I don't feel like I had to do that as much.

00:36:54.340 --> 00:36:55.360
Maybe with a few things.

00:36:55.500 --> 00:36:58.220
But, like, this felt like a game that I would just sit down and play today.

00:36:58.640 --> 00:37:00.740
And I think I would revisit this.

00:37:01.860 --> 00:37:04.880
I'm a little bummed because I can't really, I have no power here.

00:37:05.020 --> 00:37:07.360
But I am going to vote it essential.

00:37:07.520 --> 00:37:10.860
I really thought this was a hit for me.

00:37:10.860 --> 00:37:15.260
So I'm going to throw my feeble little vote towards essential.

00:37:15.800 --> 00:37:16.960
You've made your statement.

00:37:17.880 --> 00:37:19.260
That's all I needed.

00:37:19.520 --> 00:37:29.140
You know what's funny? This is the second time that a Sunsoft movie-licensed game has gotten a last-ditch essential games list vote.

00:37:29.360 --> 00:37:31.540
Sean did the same for the Batman game, actually.

00:37:31.540 --> 00:37:34.480
He was last to speak and said he's also going to throw it essential.

00:37:34.860 --> 00:37:40.640
Hey, maybe we can make some deals offline when Mike's not around about the game.

00:37:40.860 --> 00:37:42.080
That's pretty corrupt.

00:37:42.640 --> 00:37:43.700
I take my position very serious.

00:37:43.700 --> 00:37:45.120
What are we if not corrupt?

00:37:45.380 --> 00:37:51.840
Corrupt. I was actually thinking, Joe, that you were going to suggest a Batman The New Batch game.

00:37:52.280 --> 00:37:55.600
Yeah. If we combine them, they're essential.

00:37:55.880 --> 00:37:57.600
It's kind of like a Pokemon game.

00:37:57.840 --> 00:38:02.360
But instead of Batman, you play as Gizmo in the Batman world.

00:38:02.980 --> 00:38:05.320
Everybody wants to play as Electricity Batman.

00:38:06.660 --> 00:38:10.960
I want a Batman game where you just play as, what's his name, the butler.

00:38:11.460 --> 00:38:13.220
Alfred? Yeah, Alfred.

00:38:13.340 --> 00:38:15.580
And you just tell Batman where to go.

00:38:15.880 --> 00:38:16.980
Now, you said Alfred.

00:38:17.620 --> 00:38:19.520
Like Alfredo. That is his name.

00:38:19.720 --> 00:38:21.200
No, I know, but I said Alfred.

00:38:21.720 --> 00:38:25.540
You did. With like Ferderer.

00:38:26.360 --> 00:38:28.780
I don't know. I couldn't tell if that was on purpose or not.

00:38:28.980 --> 00:38:33.460
I think that was, I don't think I usually say that, but because I said it, now I'm unsure.

00:38:34.080 --> 00:38:35.980
Oh, so that wasn't on purpose?

00:38:36.000 --> 00:38:37.000
That like slipped out?

00:38:37.260 --> 00:38:38.080
Well, that's what I'm saying.

00:38:38.200 --> 00:38:40.140
Like, it's like kind of like Mario Mario.

00:38:40.540 --> 00:38:46.220
Like, I used to say it one way, now I say it the other way, and I'm just uncertain what made me cheat.

00:38:46.220 --> 00:38:50.440
Well, there is no universe where it's supposed to be Alfred.

00:38:51.260 --> 00:38:52.380
That's true. Whereas I can understand.

00:38:52.740 --> 00:38:58.140
Whereas I can understand mispronouncing Mario and Mario differently, you know?

00:38:58.140 --> 00:39:03.880
Well, just as somebody who's famous for mispronouncing things, I just feel like maybe Alfred could catch on now.

00:39:04.760 --> 00:39:07.360
You know? If, what did I used to say?

00:39:07.440 --> 00:39:09.420
Mario, right? You did say Mario.

00:39:09.640 --> 00:39:15.700
Mario. Mario caught on for a while, and there are still people around me in my circles who say Mario.

00:39:16.360 --> 00:39:28.720
Why can't Alfred become a big thing? Mario.
